{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPLEMENTATION NOTE — the plan's corpus numbers are CORRECT; the independent audit in the\nplan-review comment (146 eligible / 16 specs / 32 items / 384 case-runs) is the one that is wrong,\nand the difference is a real eligibility rule, not a rounding disagreement.\n\nMEASURED at this worktree's HEAD by the landed selector\n(`python -m rebar.llm.evals.provider_parity --dry-run`):\n\n  corpus_digest 9d707f762efbaad3bd1190373af1a878c41d801c28f7824c5a532d41eef00c2a\n  30 items, 15 gold-block + 15 gold-advisory, across 15 specs — exactly the plan's numbers.\n\nWHY THE AUDIT OVERCOUNTED. It applied the exclusion as \"everything except completion-verifier /\nticket-quality / spec-alignment\". The plan's actual rule is stronger: a case is eligible when its\nsolver id RESOLVES to a non-agentic `run_case` arm. One spec passes the loose rule and fails the\nreal one — `plan-review-isf-finder` (4 gold cases). Its solver id is neither a criterion id\n(`_criterion_id` strips the `plan-review-` prefix and looks up \"isf-finder\", which is not in the\nregistry; the registry entry is \"ISF\"), nor a `code-review-` id, nor one of the agentic three. So\n`run_case` reaches its final `raise ValueError(f\"no eval solver for prompt ...\")`. Including it\nwould not have added 4 gold items; it would have added 4 items that ERROR on BOTH arms.\n\n  146 - 4 = 142 eligible; 16 - 1 = 15 specs; 32 - 2 = 30 sampled items; 15 block / 15 advisory.\n  So the plan's 142 / 15 / 30 / 15+15 / 360 case-runs all stand as written, unchanged.\n\nThis is now enforced rather than merely observed: `solver_arm()` returns the resolved arm or\nNone, eligibility is `solver_arm(...) is not None`, and\n`test_the_isf_finder_spec_is_excluded_because_it_resolves_to_no_arm` pins it. Mutating\n`solver_arm` to the loose \"not agentic\" rule turns that test RED (verified).\n\nThe plan's worked example, `G3-R-uncovered-ac-rebar` from plan-review-container, is present in\nthe selected corpus, as the plan says it should be.\n"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785709580596758001,"uuid":"ce23dac8-27f4-4234-b6da-37b1188e275a"}